<!--Post: 3484--><!--Time: 1104959982-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3484"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Researcher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Researcher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 05, 2005 - 1:19 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The S.O.B. will be gone-gone-gone.  He will fade away back into the shadows.There will be no more comminucations from him. <BR> <BR>The bastard has defied the WPD and the feds throughout 2004.  Nothing that that he has given and submitted as clues in the past, or this year, has brought the agencies any closer to capturing him. He will go down with J.T.R and the Z - endless spectulations about who he is - never leading to an answer. <BR> <BR>That does not please me.  I want the S.O.B to be in custody and to see his mug plastered all over the media and the Internet, but I do not believe that will ever happen.  He is just to clever. <BR> <BR>As for the WPD they have released too little information and much to late. They f&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;d this up big time.  Imagine releasing an audio from BTK about Nancy Fox years after the fact - and the &#34;Oh Anna&#34; poem the same.  Even the  BTK  <BR>puzzles that the Internet community have spent so much time trying to decipher could only be done from screen captures - and poor ones at that - not complete. <BR> <BR>To think of all the communications that he has sent to the media and LE that could have been released - even in redacted form - so as not to jeapordize the investigation.... <BR> <BR>Had it not been for the civy finding the package in Murdock Park and contacting the media FIRST we might not even know that the drop contained the actual driver&#39;s license of NF. <BR> <BR>I am - by tendency - an optimist, but in this case not so.  It is easy to say - from afar - but the WPD f&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;d up and BTK was/is to smart for them and the feds. <BR> <BR>Well - if I am wrong then I will gladly eat my words. And I wanto be wrong. <BR> <BR>Now they are asking for help about a possible gift of jewelry from how many years ago?  Grasping at straws that are blowing in the wind. <BR> <BR>To little - to late.  Hope and pray that they prove me wrong and soon. <BR> <BR>What does your gut tell you???? <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3484-->
<!--Post: 3485--><!--Time: 1104963114-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3485"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 05, 2005 - 2:11 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think that the &#34;Jekyll&#34; part of BTK wants to turn himself inn, but the &#34;Hyde&#34; part doesn´t.  <BR>I think a battle between the two persons within the BTK person is raging and will continue. <BR> <BR>I think that the compromize between the two persons inside BTK is: <BR> <BR>IF!!! somone is clever/intelligent enough to find/see/decode and collect enough of the pieces that BTK have feed us with &#40;police and media and drop offs &#43; info/pictures still hidden on the web, I think&#41;and are able to create the whole picture, find the name behind it all, then BTK thinks its OK, then he will let it happen, the capture of BTK. <BR> <BR>BTK will only let a person that in some way is on his own IQ/creative-level catch him, it´s like in the fairytales, guess the 3 impossible questions and the troll will let himself be defeated. And think about WHO it is that always solve the enigma, the riddle... <BR> <BR>hugs...skov<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3485-->
<!--Post: 3491--><!--Time: 1104964225-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3491"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Brazilian<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Brazilian<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 05, 2005 - 2:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think that he&#39;ll only be identified when he die. And I dont think this day is close, as much of us think.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3491-->
<!--Post: 3502--><!--Time: 1104970153-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3502"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Researcher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Researcher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 05, 2005 - 4:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hugs back Skov.  Have read your posts with interest. <BR> <BR>My OPINION is that IQ level will have nothing to do with getting the Elusive One.  Nor do I personally believe that any clues that he has given will allow one to be able to connect the dots DIRECTLY back to him. Rather it will be a coincidence, a break out of the blue that could bring him to justice.  I do say confidently that it will NOT be the WPD who solves this case IF it is EVER solved - and unless someone comes forward with a key a new generation of LE agents will again look back with ineterst trying to solve the unsolvable.  Only this time all the parties will be long gone.  Will make an intriguing unsolved mystery for history. <BR> <BR>I do believe that all the work done by you and others in this matter is important.  It can and will become a compulsion/addiction for most, but considering the alternatives I will settle for that any day. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3502-->
<!--Post: 3507--><!--Time: 1104971585-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3507"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Gotcha<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Gotcha<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 05, 2005 - 4:33 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->You are right researcher.  All of these clues he is leaving are being purposely done to send police in the wrong direction.  I aslo believe that when he called to alert police that there was a package at Murdock Park &#40;12-8-04&#41; the package wasn&#39;t there. Police had searched and not found anything.  A week later a civilain found the package in the park.  I think he placed the package there about a week after making the call, so that the Police would look foolish.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3507-->
<!--Post: 3541--><!--Time: 1104986600-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3541"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 05, 2005 - 8:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I disagree completely that BTK is a Jeckyl/Hyde character and is imploding with conscience-driven conflict. I agree he&#39;s a legend in his own mind but this &#34;I&#39;ll let a worthy, high IQ opponent capture me&#34; attitude is childish and as written, the stuff of fairy tales. <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t know if he&#39;ll be caught in 2005, but I do know that a lot of people can do all they can to make BTK as miserable as possible. BTK should be reminded that he&#39;s mentally ill but not legally insane. I believe this is important because his early letter which addressed this topic was, IMO, a preemptive strike, a way of saying, &#34;Since I already acknowledge that I&#39;m demented, let&#39;s not go there.&#34; Just my opinion but BTK should be reminded at every opportunity that he is, indeed, mentally ill. He should also be told that he&#39;s a parody of his former self and is not feared by many in 2005. Constant pressure, even in cyberspace, can help ensure that BTK becomes his own prisoner. I&#39;d bet that this instant, BTK is much less secure and confident than he was in March or April or May. I also have a sliver of hope that he may be nailed &#40;pun intended&#41; before his anonymous, unacknowleged death. <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3541-->
<!--Post: 3545--><!--Time: 1104992234-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3545"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:josef.carlin@gmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Josef_carlin<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Josef_carlin<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 05, 2005 - 10:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->How many serial killers have been caught because they comminucated with the police? I can&#39;t think of one where the communication lead directly to the identity of the killer &#40;I am sure someone will be happy to correct me if I am mistaken&#41;. All of the captured serial killers I can think of, were caught because of evidence left at the crime scene, witnesses &#40;surviving victims&#41;, snitches, or lucky breaks. It&#39;s not that the communications have no investigative value, it&#39;s that the police tend to keep them from the public, or release it only in bits and pieces when they get desperate.  <BR> <BR>Why in the world doesn&#39;t the WPD release all the contents of all the communications? If they are going to play the BTK game why not release everything, and the sooner the better. They could keep some particulars of the crime scene secret, as investigative keys, but these communications need not be in that category. If the WPD is certain that the sticky DNA is really BTK&#39;s, why would you need to keep any investigative keys secret anyway? Afterall, the reason to keep such details secret is to eliminate false confessions &#40;if you don&#39;t know the key, your not the real killer&#41;. Since DNA can eliminate false confessions, perhaps this indicates the WPD isn&#39;t certain the DNA is his, therefore, they feel the need to retain multiple invistigative keys, just to be sure. <BR> <BR>I guess I am in the minority here. I don&#39;t think there are two sides to the killers personality. He does not want to be caught he wants the status of folklore, a legendary never ending ghost story, and he is succeeding. The necklace now has us looking not only for a middle aged man, but any women &#40;living or deceased&#41; who ever got a necklace in the late 70&#39;s. This actually increases the search, not limiting it like it might at first appear &#40;i.e. he doesn&#39;t fit the profile, but he did give me a neckalace ...&#41;.  <BR> <BR>I&#39;m pessimistic BTK will ever be caught, especially with the current practice of the WPD. Keeping the contents of the communications secret diminishes any investigative value they might have, and each time they realease a part of the contents, it sends the signal that the WPD is desperate and no closer today than they were 20 years ago. Absent a lucky break, BTK will never be caught. The best way the WPD can make their own luck in this situation is to release all the contents of the recent communications. Learn from your past mistakes and do it now before its value goes stale.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3545-->
<!--Post: 3546--><!--Time: 1104992807-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3546"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:josef.carlin@gmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Josef_carlin<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Josef_carlin<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 05, 2005 - 10:26 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Wouldn&#39;t you know it? As soon as I posted I realised that the Unibomber communication lead directly to his capture! I take some comfort in the fact that it was AFTER it was made public did they get their lucky break. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3546-->
<!--Post: 3548--><!--Time: 1104994721-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3548"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 05, 2005 - 10:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree that a data-dump by LE would be the best way to blow him out of the water, so to speak.  I would suggest that they work with Tom to showcase this stuff massively on the web.  If all the puzzles and letters and what-not &#40;redacted, as you say&#41; were dumped, there would almost certainly be somebody who would see something familiar.  And if they want BTK-level control of the goods, then they should simply set up their OWN website.  If LE is paying any attention to us, it would probably take weeks or even months to get your suggestion rolling through multiple bureaucracies.  Provided he&#39;s not caught by then, maybe we could see some real BTK data by the end of this year.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3548-->
<!--Post: 3615--><!--Time: 1105063942-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3615"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Birdieict<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Birdieict<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 06, 2005 - 6:12 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->From one of the KAKE letters: &#34;How many people do I have to kill before I get my name in the paper or some national attention?&#34; <BR> <BR>BTK is so attention-driven, it may take another lull in exposure, when the investigation goes back into the cold-case files and forgotten, to bring on more meaningful clues from him. I agree, something has happened in his life to bring him out of hiding; illness, divorce, whatever. If he outlasts WPD&#39;s attempt to follow up on these clues, the media-hungry BTK will drop an even bigger bombshell on us just when we stop searching.    <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3615-->
<!--Post: 3617--><!--Time: 1105064728-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3617"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 06, 2005 - 6:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Josef carlin- I don&#39;t know if this counts, but Ed Kemper turned himself in with a phone call. <BR>Concerning the Unabomber, Kaczynski was caught because his sister-in-law noticed odd phraseology in Ted&#39;s manifesto. Paul Michael Stephani, &#34;The Weepy-Voiced Killer,&#34; who taunted police by crying into the &#40;pay&#41; phone after murdering and saying he&#39;d never get to heaven now that he&#39;d killed again was grabbed after a 911 operator and then his sister identified his voice from a taped, tearful taunt. Of the above three serial killers, one turned himself in and the other two were captured by ordinary citizens. This might be kept in mind when folks read what BTK writes: read it, analyze it, but bear in mind that no taunting killer has ever <i>deliberately</i> placed damning information into a communique with police or media. I&#39;m afraid the same is true of BTK. I really don&#39;t think he&#39;s provided anything hugely significant in his communications, and most of his attacks were spaced, time-wise, far enough apart to the point that so many other crimes happened in between, that police, even if they had a specialized task force, were limited in what they could do. Most people thought BTK long dead or forever far away from Wichita until the Wegerle information came forward. &#40;Is it just me or does it seem strange that no crime scene photo was taken by police at the Wegerle scene?&#41;. Additionally, it seems obvious that police are seriously split in their beliefs, which isn&#39;t unusual as they are human, and I&#39;m sorry but I have to concur with the idea that human ego has played a large role in BTK remaining free. That&#39;s not as cynical or critical as it may seem; Vince Bugliosi, who prosecuted the most famous of the Manson crimes, said way back in 1974 that he believed that had not the Los Angeles Police Department and Los Angeles Co. Sherrif&#39;s Office <b>finally</b> shared their information, it was very possible Manson and the others wouldn&#39;t have even gone to trial. <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t disagree that a data-dump with only a few items needing to be redacted would be a good idea. In my opinion, it may not happen for reasons noted above. Such a dump may only underscore the clear schism which has haunted WPD since the Otero atrocity. All of this just my opinion, and it&#39;s unpopular and disconcerting because it&#39;s difficut to imagine that professionals can&#39;t put their differences aside and all go as one team after a murderer but honestly, this sort of thing happens with some frequency. I hope I&#39;m wrong, nothing would make me happier if I were. <BR> <BR>Also with a data-dump. Since the beginning, BTK has demonstrated an attempt at disguising what he wrote and, what&#39;s worse, he&#39;s kept records. This <b>doesn&#39;t</b> mean he can&#39;t be caught. The Unabomber&#39;s manifesto was over 32,000 words and it was basically one expression which ended him. BTK easily could have written an expression or nuance in his letters which someone might notice. And yes, a data-dump would need to be on a website WPD creates for itself. I simply fear it may never happen. Remember, though, that this site <i>is</i> being read by the authorities and that&#39;s not a bad thing. This site has grown, as I thought it always would. <BR> <BR>Not to put a false rainbow on things, but I do believe all hope isn&#39;t lost. With the exception of identical twins, all human beings are unique and <i>no one</i> can absolutely say that there&#39;s no chance at all. &#40;Great, now we&#39;ll have a &#34;BTK was an identical twin&#34; theory. I&#39;m joking of course; a little levity, no matter how lame, can&#39;t hurt.&#41; Sorry for such a long post but I&#39;ve ended up stating many of my truest feelings. One other thing. Wichita isn&#39;t a tiny town but it&#39;s not the vast megalopolis which many other cities are. A data-dump in &#40;and around&#41; Wichita, with an alert populace, is more likely to yield a positive result in identification than a data-dump in a larger city would. That&#39;s a stastical <i>fact.</i> Perhaps WPD is seriously considering a nearly complete data-dump? Who can say? Until then these boards are important and should be perused by any interested party.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
